      "final_text": "Done: `check_candidate` reports `VERIFIED` on all 5 requirements (all 6 kernels, 2001 property-test cases passing), and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n**Fix** ([candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean)): `VyperSqrt.sqrt` is now the deployed Babylonian loop followed by the smaller of the last two iterates (PR 4486: `if y < z: z = y`), i.e. `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)`. The old code returned the last iterate `z`, which can sit one unit above the root (e.g. raw `9999999999` for input `9999999998`); taking the minimum always lands on the floor root.\n\n**Proofs** (same file, exact locked statements, no `sorry`): the ghost Newton sequence is shown to stay in decimal range, stay above the root, halve its error each step (explicit `E/2^k + 2` bound, so error \u2264 2 after 254 steps, within one after 255 via `newton_le_sqrt_add_one`), and the loop is proved to follow the ghost sequence \u2014 so the minimum of the final pair equals `Nat.sqrt (a\u00b710^10)` in every case (early stop, fuel exhaustion, or the `10^10-1 / 10^10` seed fixed points). The three analytic requirements then follow from `Nat.sqrt_le` / `Nat.lt_succ_sqrt` via casts.\n\nPassport: [.proofforge/passport-001.json](<workspace>/.proofforge/passport-001.json), sha256 `48feae42\u2026f6ccf1`; only the permitted axioms (`Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`, `propext`) are used.",
